    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n**Open Viewing Times**\nWednesday 7th October 4.30pm - 5.00pm\nSaturday 10th October 9.30am-10am\n\nSituated within the highly sought-after Westcourt development, this beautifully renovated three-bedroom home is presented in immaculate condition throughout.\n\nBoasting an impressive B3 BER rating, the property is eligable to qualify for competitive green mortgage rates and offers a great balance of living and bedroom accommodation, making it an ideal choice for modern family living.\n\nUpon entering, the ground floor comprises a welcoming entrance hallway, a spacious living room, a bright kitchen/dining area, an office/playroom, and a generous utility room. Upstairs, there are two well-proportioned double bedrooms, a single bedroom and a stylish family bathroom.\n\nExternally, the front of the property features a gated tarmacadam driveway providing ample off-street parking. To the rear, the south-west-facing garden is fully enclosed by newly installed fencing and a bespoke contemporary privacy panel. Designed for low-maintenance outdoor living, it incorporates a stone patio, a raised lawn area and a newly installed steel garden shed offering excellent storage solutions.\n\nThe location is second to none, with a convenient pedestrian walkway from the development leading directly to the main road and a nearby bus stop. The Ballincollig By-pass Road Network is easily accessible, providing seamless connections to Bishopstown, Wilton, Cork City, and beyond. A wealth of local amenities are within walking distance, including shops, schools, cafés, restaurants, pubs, sports clubs, and the scenic Regional Park is right on the doorstep, perfect for outdoor recreation and leisurely walks.\n\nViewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHall - \nBright entrance hall, providing access to all accommodation. Enhanced by tiled flooring, this welcoming entry also features an under-stairs storage.\n\nLiving Room - 4.26m x 3.59m\nThis spacious living room, accessed directly from the hallway, features wood flooring and recessed lighting, with views overlooking the front of the property.\n\nKitchen - 6.49m x 3.86m\nEnjoy the open-plan layout in this kitchen/dining area, tiled flooring extends seamlessly throughout the space. The newly fitted kitchen features a mix of eye-level and floor-level cabinets, complemented by a tiled backsplash. Integrated appliances, including an oven, hob, and fridge, add modern convenience, all illuminated by recessed lighting. A door leads to the utility room, providing access to the rear garden and allowing for an effortless transition from indoor to outdoor living.\n\nUtility Room - 2.77m x 5.64m\nThis generous area, originally the kitchen before the renovation, now serves as a utility space with ample storage units, a sink, and plumbing for a washing machine and dryer. A door provides direct access to the rear garden, while the space also offers a secondary entrance to the playroom/office space at the front of the house.\n\nPlayroom/office space - 2.74m x 2.44m\nAn extra room at the front of the house, currently used as a playroom, can easily be converted into an office to suit the needs of a modern family.\n\nLanding - \nProvides access to all bedrooms, as well as a Stira ladder leading to the semi-floored attic space.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.68m x 4.20m\nThis bedroom offers views of the expansive green area and Inniscarra in the distance through a large window. It features carpet flooring and a floor-to-ceiling built-in wardrobe with recessed lighting.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.66m x 3.31m\nThis generously sized double bedroom boasts wood flooring, and a window offering views over the rear of the property.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.64m x 3.16m\nThis single room offers views overlooking the front of the property and is adorned with wood flooring.\n\nBathroom - 2.66m x 1.88m\nThree-piece bath suite with power shower, the floor and surrounding walls are tiled.\n\n"
      },
